      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "be the meaning here. गर्भ still presents a difficulty. For rendering",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "it by चित्त I know of no authority. With मुख for हुत it is easy to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "explain but मुख cannot be well construed with what follows.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "I would translate thus, “the vicinity of which is darkened by the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "smoke of the fire to which offerings are made by Brahmins",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "having within them (i. e. their mouths) the Vedic accents (i.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "e. Vedic Mantras with their due accent). वरम् is the predicate",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "in the first clause of this Stanza, all the other adjectives are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "extensions of the subject. तुल्यकुल्य = तुल्याः स्वकुलभवाः (Râmarshi)",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "better, perhaps, would have been तुल्यकुले भवाः but this is in-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "admissible. See Siddh. Kaum. I., 514.—Sragdharâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LVI.—तत्त्व &c. = तत्त्वनिवेशेन तत्त्वज्ञानेन पेशला सुकुमारा करुणार्द्रा म-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "तिर्बुद्धिर्यस्य स तथाभूतः (Râmarshi) better, I think “ one whose mind",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "is skilled in concentration on the truth.” तत्त्व in Gîtâ II., 16 is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "explained by S'ankara as ब्रह्मयाथात्म्यम् and by S'rîdhara as वस्तुया-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "थार्थ्यम् which two are not inconsistent. That meaning may be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "adopted here ; for निवेश comp. Misc. St. 19. पेशल = clever. उत्पत्न",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "&c. = उत्पन्ना उदिता विकल्पजल्पाः वितर्कवचनानि येषां ते उत्पत्नविकल्पजल्पा अत",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "एव मुखराः दुर्मुखाः (Râmarshi.); better, I think, जल्पैर्मुखराः as in Nîtis'a-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "taka St. 69. स्वयम् = स्वेनैव रूपेण आनन्दवन्त इत्यर्थः (Râmarshi) but",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "“ by themselves” is, I think, quite admissible.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LVII.—व्यतिकर. See St. 52. चित्तान्तः &c. is not clear. It",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "may be “ into whose minds worldly objects which are like a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "dangerous snake have entered,” but there is a difficulty of both",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "grammar and sense in this. The reading of B. (taking अचि-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "न्वन्तो) would mean “ not looking to (i. e. not minding) the course",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "of worldly objects which are like dangerous snakes.” आभोग =",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "expanse, Uttararâmacharita p. 42. नयन्ते. The Âtmanepada is only",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "for the metre. सुकृत &c. comp. St. 49.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LVIII.—इन्द्रियार्थ = objects of sense i. e. worldly objects.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
